WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.970
I want to talk a little bit about a piece
that Joel Mathes wrote in the week about how

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:13.290
Donald Trump just can't stand, that Joe Biden
is stealing the spotlight from him and Trump's

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.420
been hiding out at the White House and at
his golf courses.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.539
But that's actually making the problem even
worse.

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:24.570
And Joe Mathes in his piece likens it to Norma
Desmond in Sunset Boulevard.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:30.420
And you might remember in Sunset Boulevard,
Norma Desmond is she ends up long after she

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:35.010
is no longer, you know, the Hollywood star
that she once was.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:41.380
She's surrounded by sycophants and enablers
and yes, men and yes, women, long after she

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:46.780
stops commanding any respect, sort of living
out a fantasy, living out a fake existence

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.330
for lack of a better term.

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:54.401
And the point the analogy here is that Donald
Trump's behavior only makes sense if you go

00:00:54.401 --> 00:01:00.760
beyond questions like could this strategy
work to steal the election from Joe Biden?

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:05.470
Does Trump really think that he actually won
Pennsylvania?

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:10.159
Once you get beyond those initial questions
and you go to, well, what Trump is doing here

00:01:10.159 --> 00:01:17.420
is desperately trying to cling to the spotlight,
both for ego and vanity, as much as fears

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:22.200
of being investigated and potentially prosecuted
after he's out of office.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.520
That's the framework in which this starts
to make sense.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.830
And the more that the spotlight turns towards
Joe Biden, the angrier that Donald Trump gets,

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:36.170
which explains his tweets over the weekend
saying, why is Joe Biden forming a cabinet?

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:42.370
Why is Joe Biden moving ahead when we still
are fighting this and we actually won?

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:47.460
And the reality is that this is when the spotlight
should be turning to Joe Biden for two reasons.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:48.460
No.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:55.439
One, in general, when you have a new president
elect, the president that's outgoing is called

00:01:55.439 --> 00:01:56.610
a lame duck president.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:01.610
That's because while they are still president,
the next four years are going to be decided

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:08.310
upon from an executive, from the executive
branch standpoint, by Joe Biden, not by Donald

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.310
Trump.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.939
And so Donald Trump has these waning days
during which he is president.

00:02:11.939 --> 00:02:16.019
So in general, the attention now turns to
the president elect.

00:02:16.019 --> 00:02:17.879
What is the cabinet going to look like?

00:02:17.879 --> 00:02:19.370
What are the day one priorities?

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:22.109
What are the 100 day priorities, et cetera?

00:02:22.109 --> 00:02:28.169
But Donald Trump is exacerbating the speed
at which the spotlight is turning to Joe Biden

00:02:28.169 --> 00:02:30.760
because Donald Trump isn't even working anymore.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.090
Trump stop doing presidential work.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:39.150
Months before the election, he was just campaigning,
not dealing with coronavirus, not getting

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.870
his PDB presidential daily briefings.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:44.620
And he's barely been seen in public since
the election.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:47.930
He's scheduled to do some kind of turkey thing
today related to Thanksgiving.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:50.459
He's not actually taking questions since the
election.

00:02:50.459 --> 00:02:53.819
It's probably been about a month since he's
taken press questions.

00:02:53.819 --> 00:02:57.309
We have one hundred year pandemic, which Trump
all but ignored.

00:02:57.309 --> 00:03:01.379
And Joe Biden has a coronavirus task force
and is taking it seriously.

00:03:01.379 --> 00:03:04.749
So, of course, Americans in the media are
turning to Joe Biden.

00:03:04.749 --> 00:03:08.980
If you look at Joe Biden and Trump, only one
of them is still dealing with coronavirus

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.059
or is dealing with coronavirus.

00:03:11.059 --> 00:03:12.059
And it's Joe Biden.

00:03:12.059 --> 00:03:13.480
So who are you going to turn to?

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:17.939
Joe Biden is the one choosing a cabinet that
is going to have to lead us out of this mess

00:03:17.939 --> 00:03:20.409
economically and from a public health standpoint.

00:03:20.409 --> 00:03:23.379
So, of course, that's what we're talking about
and evaluating.

00:03:23.379 --> 00:03:25.749
Is Joe Biden making the right choices or not?

00:03:25.749 --> 00:03:29.480
And how are these people going to govern that
Joe Biden is selecting?

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:34.989
So when Trump doesn't recognize Biden's win,
finally now allowing the formal transition

00:03:34.989 --> 00:03:39.310
to start, which is the closest we're going
to get to a concession from Trump while still

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:44.279
claiming that he actually won, he is desperately
trying to cling not just to the.

00:03:44.279 --> 00:03:49.330
Presidency, but to the spotlight because of
his ego and his narcissism and Joel Mathis

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:57.839
does point out that some of this is the media's
fault by continuing to talk about Joe Biden's

00:03:57.839 --> 00:04:05.909
apparent victory and the network, the networks
like OEI and a Newsmax, not even using the

00:04:05.909 --> 00:04:12.529
term apparent victor and just placating any
insane notion about Donald Trump being the

00:04:12.529 --> 00:04:17.669
actual winner, they do encourage the system
to keep it going.

00:04:17.669 --> 00:04:20.329
But it's mostly Donald Trump.

00:04:20.329 --> 00:04:22.930
And we know Trump hates being ridiculed.

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:25.169
We know Trump hates being mocked.

00:04:25.169 --> 00:04:30.820
And we saw that with his quick distancing
from that whacked out lawyer, Sydney Powell,

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:36.050
when she went on Newsmax and said there would
be evidence of biblical proportions soon to

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:37.590
prove fraud.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.009
She was instantly fired.

00:04:39.009 --> 00:04:41.000
And in fact, it was one of these retroactive.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:46.289
She never really was working for us anyway
because the mockery is what got to Donald

00:04:46.289 --> 00:04:48.009
Trump that does actually get to him.

00:04:48.009 --> 00:04:54.970
So it's possible that more mockery of Trump
will get him to do more to maybe to actually

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:58.480
use the term I concede and call Joe Biden.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:03.719
But all that really matters is that Donald
Trump yesterday did finally say via Twitter,

00:05:03.719 --> 00:05:08.699
I'm allowing the transition to happen formally,
even though I'm going to keep fighting.

00:05:08.699 --> 00:05:12.330
And eventually Donald Trump will leave regardless.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:16.620
Joe Biden will still become president, but
it's going to be all the more embarrassing

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:17.840
for Donald Trump.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:24.490
In the meantime, the best we can do is all
move on to talking about Joe Biden's plans,

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:28.389
his cabinet selections, his coronavirus task
force.

00:05:28.389 --> 00:05:29.509
And we're doing it.

00:05:29.509 --> 00:05:35.860
And I have to tell you, I am as I've said
before, Trump would be better.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:39.270
Another four years of Trump would be better
for the business of The David Pakman Show.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:42.610
There's no doubt it would be worse for the
country.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:49.139
And I am actually enjoying starting to look
into the backgrounds of Joe Biden's cabinet

00:05:49.139 --> 00:05:50.289
picks.

00:05:50.289 --> 00:05:54.530
What is Joe Biden likely to do on day one
via executive order?

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:58.710
What is Biden going to do in his first week
in terms of the virus?

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:00.509
What are the first 100 day priorities?

00:06:00.509 --> 00:06:06.860
How is Biden's secretary of Homeland Security
going to deal with immigration policy?

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:09.710
We're actually getting back into substance.

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:13.830
And I heard from a bunch of people yesterday,
longtime viewers of the show, who have said,

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:15.690
you know, I've been a fan for a long time.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:20.629
I love what you do, but I am already feeling
a breath of fresh air and just getting back

00:06:20.629 --> 00:06:23.990
to talking about policy, even if we don't
agree with everything Joe Biden does.

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:25.729
Certainly we will not.

00:06:25.729 --> 00:06:29.370
The guy who looked at the solar eclipse, his
time is up.

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:34.669
The guy who suggested bleach injections, sort
of like a cleaning to treat the virus.

00:06:34.669 --> 00:06:40.770
He is going to be leaving the guy who used
the Sharpie to adjust a hurricane map for

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:42.139
political gain.

00:06:42.139 --> 00:06:44.620
He is exiting stage left in eight weeks.

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:47.180
And we are all the better for it.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.879
And we are we are going to continue moving
forward.

00:06:49.879 --> 00:06:56.970
And I am glad to say that hopefully progressive
media is on the path to becoming dramatically

00:06:56.970 --> 00:07:02.610
more substantive as we get closer and closer
to Joe Biden's swearing in.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:06.169
Make sure you're following us on Instagram
at David Pakman show.

00:07:06.169 --> 00:07:49.360
And while you're there, you can follow me
on Instagram at David Pakman 

00:07:49.360 --> 00:08:21.569
as well.

